   "sentenceId": 22,
   "he": "סָפֵק וְאַנְדְּרוֹגִינוֹס כּוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״עׇרְלָתוֹ״ — עׇרְלָתוֹ וַדַּאי דּוֹחֶה אֶת הַשַּׁבָּת,",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: If there is «uncertainty» whether or not to circumcise a baby, «and» likewise in the case of «a hermaphrodite» baby, one does not desecrate Shabbat to perform the circumcision of «a hermaphrodite,» even on the eighth day following the birth. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states: “And on the eighth day the flesh of his foreskin shall be circumcised” (Leviticus 12:3), and they interpreted the verse: «“His foreskin”» indicates that only the circumcision of «his» halakhically «certain foreskin overrides Shabbat,»"
  }
 ],
